      "holding": "No. Following Ashok Kumar & Others v. State of U.P., Clause 6.8 requires: (a) a site inspection report disclosing the irregularity, handed to the consumer or pasted/posted if refused; (b) a show-cause notice with the provisional assessment, giving 15 working days for reply and fixing a hearing date; and (c) after personal hearing, a speaking final order within 7 working days recording whether unauthorised use is established and the assessed amount. Since no such show-cause notice was issued and no final order under Clause 6.8(c) was passed, a bill-cum-notice and demand notice issued instead under Section 5 of the 1958 Act is illegal and inconsistent with the prescribed procedure; it is set aside, without prejudice to the licensee proceeding afresh in accordance with the Clause 6.8/Ashok Kumar procedure.",
